      "stageRecord": "Project a declarative CP with a silent C and place the separately constructed DP Ces lettres in Spec-CP. Coindex this left-dislocated DP with the object-clitic chain. Spec-CP c-commands the resumptive clitic and its lower trace, establishing the local A′ topic-resumption dependency. Ces lettres is base-generated in the left periphery: it does not move from the object position, and it is not an additional verbal argument. The Theme role remains on the clitic chain. Because the topic is outside IP, its relation to the pronominal clitic does not violate the local freedom requirement associated with Principle B; the lower head-movement trace is licensed within the clitic chain. The completed interpretation is that, as for these letters, Léa sent them to Paul. The comma marks the left-dislocation boundary and the period marks the declarative boundary; neither punctuation mark is a supplied word token.",
